+%%%%
+Weave Enchantments
+
+Move a complete artifact enchantment into your personal archive or onto a
+compatible recipient. The donor survives, depleted. Your bound enchantments
+share at most six capacity, with one thread per property and normally one per
+item. A Masterwork holds two threads within the same budget.
+
+Drawbacks reserve capacity even in the archive and can be restored to their
+donor. Brands replace the recipient's active brand. Unique powers retain their
+native state and cost all six capacity. Borrowed powers require your equipped
+recipient and Vellum's favour. Trading or consuming an item cannot copy them.
+
+The menu shows exact eligibility, capacity and piety costs. Ordinary work takes
+five of your own actions and commits only when complete; interruption spends
+nothing. The starter gift and destruction/restoration of a thread take one
+action. Overweave is not part of this ability.
+%%%%
+Chain Lash ability
+
+Strike one visible hostile within three tiles with a bodily chain. A successful physical hit deals 1d(5 + XL/3) damage before armour and may tether an eligible body, even if armour absorbs all the damage. The original distance becomes the chain's maximum length; the foe can move within it and still attack or cast. Lash lasts four, six or eight standard turns at XL1, XL7 or XL13. One chain can be maintained at a time. A miss or ended hold begins five turns of recovery.
+%%%%
+Reel In ability
+
+Consume your existing mobile tether and physically pull its target up to two consecutive cells toward you, stopping at adjacency or the first obstruction. A foe at range three ends adjacent on a clear path. There is no second accuracy or Willpower roll, added damage, stun or free attack. An adjacent target or a visibly blocked pull spends nothing and preserves the hold.
+%%%%
+Pinning Chain ability
+
+Replace your mobile tether with a fixed anchor at its target's current solid-floor cell. The target can move within one tile of the anchor. The pin lasts at most four standard turns and never extends the original hold. At least two turns must remain before activation. Pinning requires XL13 and uses the existing target without another selection.
+%%%%
+Release Chain ability
+
+Release your one living chain instantly and begin the same five-turn recovery as any other ending. Walking beyond a mobile tether's reach releases it automatically. Releasing never resets or shortens recovery.
+%%%%
+Profane Altar ability
+
+At an available god's own altar, permanently steal its single offered benefit and accept its wrath. Choose at most three distinct gods. The first theft supplies forty Defiance once; later thefts never refill it. Duplicate and ecumenical altars grant nothing. Profanation does not consume the altar or prevent an ally from worshipping there.
+%%%%
+Invoke Elder Rites ability
+
+At XL9, XL15 and XL21, complete one short two-wave encounter to strengthen all your stolen benefits. Begin on safe open ground. The second wave arrives after four standard turns without waiting for the first wave to die. Trial actors grant no rewards. Killing or permanently banishing every trial actor wins; pacification, conversion and dismissal do not. Leaving the floor abandons the attempt, preserving completed rites. Only one party rite can be active on a floor.
