 Vorr reopens the wounds of those who abandon the Red Wake. Bloodless bodies
 cannot bleed even under divine wrath.
+
+%%%%
+Vellum
+
+Vellum, the Archbinder, sees every enchantment as a thread awaiting a worthy
+place. Followers may lift enchantments from artifacts and bind them to other
+artifacts. The source survives, depleted. Each thread exists only once.
+
+Vellum rewards victories over worthy foes. Enchanting, trading and hoarding
+items never earn favour.
+%%%%
+Vellum powers
+
+One free starter thread and an apprentice vessel make the first binding
+possible before finding two artifacts. Earned devotion increases personal
+capacity from one to six. Capacity remains unlocked when piety is spent.
+Normally an item holds one imported thread; six-star followers can designate
+one Masterwork with room for two. The six-capacity total remains unchanged.
+
+Any nonzero native artifact enchantment may be extracted, including drawbacks,
+brands and unique powers. Unique powers are conserved as complete native
+behaviour bundles and cost six capacity. Recipients must support the effect.
+Over-capacity threads may wait in the archive. Drawbacks reserve capacity even
+in the archive; restoring one ends its thread and returns it to the donor.
+A drawback is suppressed only while its original owner carries the donor
+under Vellum's favour. This prevents permanent purification or party-wide gifts.
+
+An imported property never stacks additively with the same native property;
+brands replace the active brand. Weapon and armour enchantment levels also
+move intact, at one capacity per level. Ordinary base-item subtype properties
+remain intrinsic. Named artifacts unlock at five stars. Invocations skill is
+not required.
+
+Extraction costs 2 plus twice the lesser of six and the thread's capacity.
+Moving a thread costs three piety. Most work takes five of your own actions.
+Danger, interruption, or stale item state cancels it without spending piety or
+enchantments. Exact consequences are shown before permanent extraction.
+%%%%
+Vellum wrath
+
+Vellum launches no separate attacks against former followers. Borrowed power
+becomes dormant without divine favour, and suppressed drawbacks return.
+Bindings and earned capacity remain recorded if the follower returns.
